    "DECISIONS": "Adopted the ASC 606 concept for years 2018–present alongside the legacy concept; legacy concept alone appropriate for 2011‑2017.",
    "CONTEXT": "Evidence shows a clear shift in concept usage aligned with ASC 606 adoption, with concurrent reporting after 2018."
  },
  "answer": {
    "summary": "Tesla initially used only the legacy 'Revenues' concept (2011‑2017). Starting in 2018 it began also reporting under the ASC 606 concept 'RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax', reflecting the revenue‑recognition standard change. Both concepts appear together in regular filings, not amended ones, indicating intentional dual tagging rather than errors. Which concept to use depends on the analyst’s need: 'Revenues' for total GAAP revenue; the ASC 606 concept for contract revenue excluding assessed tax.",
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "From 2011 through 2017 Tesla reported revenue only under the 'Revenues' concept, with fact counts of 22 in 2011 and 21 each year 2012‑2017.",
        "evidence": ["E-59c5aa"]
      },
      {
        "text": "In 2018 Tesla first reported under the ASC 606 concept 'RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax' (6 facts) while continuing to report under 'Revenues' (21 facts).",
        "evidence": ["E-59c5aa"]
      },
      {
        "text": "Accession numbers containing both concepts are regular filings (form_type values such as 10-K, 10-Q) with no '/A' suffix, refuting the duplicate‑tagging via amended filings hypothesis.",
        "evidence": ["E-d1d862"]
      },
      {
        "text": "The same accession numbers with both concepts appear across multiple years (e.g., 0001564590-19-003165, 0001628280-24-002390), indicating the dual tagging is not an isolated early error.",
        "evidence": ["E-0e3ef9"]
      }
    ],
    "inferences": [
      {
        "text": "The dual concepts likely reflect the ASC 606 requirement to disclose revenue from customer contracts excluding assessed taxes, allowing users to view both total GAAP revenue and tax‑excluded contract revenue.",
        "basis": "Claims about the timing of concept introduction (2018) aligning with ASC 606 adoption and the continued presence of the legacy 'Revenues' concept for total revenue."
      }
    ],
    "hypothesis_verdicts": [
      {
        "id": "H-3b9440",
        "status": "supported",
        "evidence": ["E-0e3ef9", "E-763045", "E-a6bd98"],
        "why": "Shows a shift from exclusive use of 'Revenues' (2011‑2017) to concurrent use of both concepts starting 2018, consistent with ASC 606 adoption."
      },
      {
        "id": "H-d0b0d7",
        "status": "refuted",
        "evidence": ["E-d1d862"],
        "why": "Accession numbers with both concepts are regular 10-K/10-Q filings, not amended filings, so duplicate tagging is not due to A‑filings."
      },
